# `integ::IntegraOptions`

The strategy of `integra` and the settings of its two engines.

`strategy` chooses the engine; `quadrature` and `monte_carlo` are the full option structs of the two engines, used when that engine runs. In `Auto`, the quadrature tolerance and refinement budget decide when quadrature has failed, so tightening them sends more integrals to Monte Carlo.

## Fields

### `strategy`

`integ::IntegraStrategy`, default `Auto`.

The engine.

### `quadrature`

`integ::QuadraOptions`, default `{}`.

Settings of the quadrature engine.

### `monte_carlo`

`integ::AleatoriaOptions`, default `{}`.

Settings of the Monte Carlo engine.

## Guidance

Passed to `integra`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

Settings of each engine.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace integ = pluss::subsp::math::integ;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(10));
  integ::IntegraOptions options;
  options.quadrature.rule = integ::QuadraRule::GaussLegendre;
  options.quadrature.tolerance = 1e-12;
  options.monte_carlo.samples = 100000;
  const integ::IntegraResult r = integ::integra([](const Series &t) { return t.sin(); }, 0.0, 3.14159265358979323846, options);
  out.writeln("value =", r.value.item<double>(), ", evaluations =", r.evaluations);
}
```

### Example 2

A tight tolerance sends the integral to Monte Carlo when quadrature cannot reach it in its budget.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace integ = pluss::subsp::math::integ;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(8));
  integ::IntegraOptions options;
  options.quadrature.tolerance = 1e-15;
  options.quadrature.max_refinements = 0;
  options.quadrature.nodes = 5;
  options.monte_carlo.samples = 50000;
  options.monte_carlo.seed = 2;
  const integ::IntegraResult r = integ::integra([](const Series &t) { return t.exp(); }, 0.0, 1.0, options);
  out.writeln("strategy used =", static_cast<int>(r.strategy_used), ", converged =", r.converged, ", error estimate =", r.error_estimate);
}
```

### Example 3

Monte Carlo only, with a seed.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace integ = pluss::subsp::math::integ;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(6));
  integ::IntegraOptions options;
  options.strategy = integ::IntegraStrategy::MonteCarlo;
  options.monte_carlo.samples = 30000;
  options.monte_carlo.seed = 10;
  const integ::IntegraResult r = integ::integra([](const Series &t) { return t; }, 0.0, 2.0, options);
  out.writeln("value =", r.value.item<double>(), ", exact = 2, error estimate =", r.error_estimate);
}
```

